Newt Todo — third-party attributions
=====================================

Design palette & UX inspiration: gitdeck
----------------------------------------
The dark design system in this app (the color/surface/accent/shadow palette)
and the sidebar app-shell layout are adapted from gitdeck.

  Project: gitdeck
  Source:  https://github.com/debba/gitdeck
  Branch:  feat/multi-account-provider
  Files referenced: src/styles/tokens.css, src/styles/layout-sidebar.css,
                    src/components/AccountSwitcher.tsx (look/feel inspiration)
  License: MIT (Copyright (c) debba)

The MIT License permits this reuse with attribution. gitdeck's palette was
re-expressed as a native Tailwind v4 theme (an `@theme` block in src/app.css),
preserving the exact hex/rgba values; no gitdeck CSS file is bundled. The shell
markup was re-implemented for this app's data model rather than copied verbatim.

Dashboard view structure & filter/sort logic: gitdeck
-----------------------------------------------------
The Repos / Issues / Pull Requests dashboard sections port gitdeck's view
STRUCTURE and behavior — not its CSS. Reference files:

  src/components/views/{RepoGrid,IssueList,PullRequestList}.tsx
  src/utils/dashboard.ts   (filter / sort logic)
  src/utils/format.ts      (formatRelativeTime, formatNumber)
  src/utils/colors.ts      (GitHub label color handling)
  License: MIT (Copyright (c) debba) — https://github.com/debba/gitdeck

The dense-row layout, field selection, label-color handling, relative-time
formatting and the issue/PR filter+sort helpers were re-implemented for this
app's data model and re-rendered with this app's Tailwind v4 design tokens and
Lucide icons. Specifically: src/lib/dashboard.ts adapts the filter/sort logic;
src/lib/format.ts adapts formatRelativeTime and the label-color helper; and
src/components/dashboard/{IssueList,PullRequestList,RepoGrid,listRow}.tsx adapt
the view structure. No gitdeck source files are copied verbatim or bundled.
